{"At \003four\004 you can go into the greenhouse and get two dozen daffodils to remind us of spring, that there is a spring.","Bright Valley of Love","Edna Hong",true},
{"It was \003four o’clock\004, and they had another hour of daylight left before it would be time to quit. Charlie wanted to shoot his father’s gun as promised, though not at a duck, but he didn’t know if he dared ask.","Blue Springs","Peter Rennebohm",true},
{"I followed his gaze to the mantelpiece. The clock had stopped at \003four o’clock\004.\n“Mon ami, someone has tampered with it. It had still three days to run. It is an eight-day clock, you comprehend?”\n“But what should they want to do that for? Some idea of a false scent by making the crime appear to have taken place at four o’clock?”","The Big Four","Agatha Christie",true},
{"It’s a delusional painter who finishes a canvas at two o’clock and expects radical societal transformation by \003four\004. Even when artists write manifestos, they are (hopefully) aware that their exigent tone is, finally, borrowed, only echoing and mimicking the urgency of the guerrilla’s demands, or the activist’s protests, rather than truly enacting it. The people sometimes demand change. They almost never demand art.","Intimations","Zadie Smith",true},
{"“If ever you are passing my way,” said Bilbo, “don’t wait to knock! Tea is at \003four\004, but any of you are welcome at any time.”","The Hobbit","J.R.R. Tolkien",true},
{"At \003four clock\004, Eva unspools the finished Harvard reference from her typewriter, folds it neatly, and places it inside a good cream envelope. Then she shrugs on her coat, checks her handbag for car keys, purse, compact.","Versions of Us","Laura Barnett",true},
{"But, with a throb of undiluted angst, I realized that I’d felt such restlessness and emptiness in the past. Often. It usually kicked in at about \003four o’clock\004 on a Sunday, but had arrived slightly late today, no doubt still on New York time.","Rachel’s Holiday","Marian Keyes",true},
{"It was \003four o’clock\004 before we finally got away. Now, for some reason, it was Charles and Camilla who weren’t speaking. They’d fought about something — I’d seen them arguing in the yard — and all the way home, in the back seat, they sat side by side and stared straight ahead, their arms folded across their chests in what I am sure they did not realize was a comically identical fashion.","The Secret History","Donna Tartt",true},
{"Sammy woke, flushed and disoriented, around \003four\004 that afternoon. We made our tea together. I put on bread to toast and I put soup in a pan to heat. Outside the weather worsened, tumbling up into a spring storm, all squalls and blusters. Sammy rode on my hip and we made a game of it as I walked around the house checking the window fixings and drawing the curtains, even though it wasn’t yet properly dark.","The Body Lies","Jo Baker",true},
{"They stood at the iron rail, not talking among themselves, just watching. And taking long slow deep breaths, like tourists from the Midwest standing for the first time on Pemaquid Point or Quoddy Head in Maine, breathing deep of the fresh sea air. As a sign of respect, Rose took off her tophat and held it by her side.\nAt \003four o’clock\004 they trooped back to their encampment in the parking lot, invigorated. They would return the next day, and the day after that, and the day after that. They would return until the good steam was exhausted, and then they would move on.","Doctor Sleep","Stephen King",true},
{"“Good morning, Dr. Tuttle,” I said.\n“It’s \003four in the afternoon\004,” she said. “I’m sorry it took me so long to return your call. My cats had an emergency. Are you feeling better? The symptoms you described in your message, frankly, puzzle me.”","My Year of Rest and Relaxation","Ottessa Moshfegh",true},
{"Well, it had become pretty clear I wasn’t going to be able to catch E. on her own. She never appeared at the belfry at \003four P.M.\004 That my communiqués were being intercepted was the only explanation that occurred to me.","Cloud Atlas","David Mitchell",true},
{"I propose myself the satisfaction of waiting on you and your family, Monday, November 18th, by \003four o’clock\004, and shall probably trespass on your hospitality till the Saturday se’ennight following, which I can do without any inconvenience, as Lady Catherine is far from objecting to my occasional absence on a Sunday, provided that some other clergyman is engaged to do the duty of the day.","Pride and Prejudice","Jane Austen",true},
{"“At \003four o’clock\004, therefore, we may expect this peace-making gentleman,” said Mr. Bennet, as he folded up the letter.","Pride and Prejudice","Jane Austen",true},
{"It was nearly \003four o’clock\004 when we at last, after passing through the beautiful Stroud Valley, and over the broad gleaming Severn, found ourselves at the pretty little country-town of Ross. A lean, ferret-like man, furtive and sly-looking, was waiting for us upon the platform.","The Adventures of Sherlock Holmes","Sir Arthur Conan Doyle",true},
{"She lay down at \003four o’clock\004, not expecting to sleep a wink, but her healing body had its own priorities. She went under almost instantly, and when she woke to the insistent \001dah-dah-dah\002 of her bedside clock, she was glad she had set the alarm. Outside, a gusty October breeze was combing leaves from the trees and sending them across her backyard in colorful skitters. The light had gone that strange and depthless gold which seems the exclusive property of late-fall afternoons in New England.","Full Dark, No Stars","Stephen King",true},
{"So then my father refused to eat Christmas lunch with us, which my mother finally served at around \003four p.m.\004, by which time we were all starving and quite drunk, and, well … it was a very dysfunctional Christmas Day.","Apples Never Fall","Liane Moriarty",true},
{"That’s enough to begin with, Humpty Dumpty interrupted: “there are plenty of hard words there. ‘Brillig’ means \003four o’clock in the afternoon\004 — the time when you begin broiling things for dinner.”","Through the Looking Glass","Lewis Carroll",true},
{"Please join us on Sunday February 2nd 2003 from \0034 p.m.\004 at the Hoxton Gallery, London N1, to preview a new exhibition of faecal paintings by Catherine Leidensteiner.","Adrian Mole and the Weapons of Mass Destruction","Sue Townsend",false},
{"Billy Bibbit and his girl mentioned that it was after \003four o’clock\004 and, if it was all right, if people didn’t mind, they’d like to have Mr. Turkle unlock the Seclusion Room.","One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest","Ken Kesey",true},
{"“If you should have no objection to receive me into your house,\nI propose myself the satisfaction of waiting on you and your family,\nMonday, November 18th, by \003four o’clock\004, and shall probably trespass\non your hospitality till the Saturday se’ennight following, which I can\ndo without any inconvenience, as Lady Catherine is far from objecting\nto my occasional absence on a Sunday, provided that some other clergyman is engaged to do the duty of the day.”","Pride and Prejudice","Jane Austen",true},
{"Later in the morning, and just as the girls were going to separate in preparation for the regular \003four o’clock\004 dinner, the hero of this inimitable charade walked in again.","Emma","Jane Austen",true},
{"“Think of me to-morrow, my dear Emma, about \003four o’clock\004,” was Mrs. Weston’s parting injunction; spoken with some anxiety, and meant only for her.","Emma","Jane Austen",true},
{"The afternoon waned from the purging good of three o’clock to the golden beauty of \003four\004.","This Side of Paradise","F. Scott Fitzgerald",true},
{"… when they all sat down to table at \003four o’clock\004, about three hours after his arrival, he had secured his lady, engaged her mother’s consent, and was not only in the rapturous profession of the lover, but, in the reality of reason and truth, one of the happiest of men.","Sense and Sensibility","Jane Austen",true},
{"What else can I answer, When the lights come on at \003four\004 At the end of another year","The Whitsun Weddings","Philip Larkin",true},
{"\0034:00 p.m.\004 Take Toby out of his cage","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon",true},
{"As he turned off towards the fishing village of Cellardyke, the familiar pips announced the \003four o’clock\004 news. The comforting voice of the newsreader began the bulletin. “The convicted serial killer and former TV chat show host Jacko Vance has begun his appeal against conviction.”","The Last Temptation","Val McDermid",true},
{"Charmian woke at \003four\004 and sensed the emptiness of the house.","Memento Mori","Muriel Spark",true},
