{"It was \003nearly five\004 in the evening when the cook came aboard. He did not have the cabbages.","A Single Pebble","John Hershey",true},
{"After an hour, they caught one gold-and-brown-striped fish that was kind of small, and they put him back. Prager swore it was a baby walleye; Eva seemed fairly sure it wasn’t.\nAfter another hour of drowning worms and losing them in little nibbles, it was \003almost 5:00 p.m.\004, and supposedly the best time to catch walleye was in the evening; clearly, they were just too eager and had started too early.","Kitchens of the Great Midwest","J. Ryan Stradal",true},
